{"artifacts":{"architecture-governor.json":{"sha256":"745fc34fbbb440a293ecd61d49bc36ebc0c0a5a18eda640d9640b9ae15037651","text":"{\"context_sha256\":\"674a06476636c493cb59dc93f93505743dff5b622665f990f3e4107dcff7d7fd\",\"contract_sha256\":\"1e4872c41bedc71ca8e0210062d87b20f0b7c8a12d8843d5ada96bdcef2ef63b\",\"convergence\":\"improves\",\"debts\":[\"DEBT-CHAT-AREA\"],\"decision\":\"proceed\",\"design_sha256\":\"b12a6976956859c6e8671faf313c3183da72f643b7badf40fad1b106dbbacd02\",\"migrations\":[\"MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS\"],\"policy_sha256\":\"0db30c9f1e05383df234c84feb31dcef348f09ec605db423606b9f72c7e54add\",\"principles\":[\"ARCH-DEEP-MODULES\",\"ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES\"],\"rationale\":[\"Named, testable seam: AC-1/AC-2/AC-4 map to CitationModal's mount-effect-with-cleanup, provable through the public interface (render, unmount, document.activeElement) without reaching into internals.\",\"Behaviour sits behind the seam, not in front of it: opener capture, Close-button focus and the detached-opener guard all live inside CitationModal's lifecycle; the caller needs no new props, callbacks or state, so no orchestration is pushed onto ChatArea.\",\"Interface stays small: CitationModal's public signature is unchanged, no new exports, refs or configuration knobs are exposed, and no new npm dependency is introduced.\",\"The design extends the existing deep module rather than adding a parallel one: planned_files is CitationModal.tsx only, allowed_new_files is empty, and it follows AddVideoModal's established focus-on-open precedent instead of inventing a new abstraction.\",\"No parallel-seam risk: no focus-return hook or util exists in app/frontend/src/hooks or lib (verified), and inline modal-lifecycle focus is the codebase's existing pattern; a one-off useFocusReturn hook for a single caller would be a speculative abstraction under ARCH-DEEP-MODULES.\",\"DEBT-CHAT-AREA and MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS are respected: ChatArea.tsx and Message.tsx are untouched; had opener capture/restore been pushed into ChatArea, it would have grown the no-growth hotspot and worked against the active migration.\",\"Layer direction intact: CitationModal stays in frontend-components using only React built-ins, adds no import edges, and keeps UI behaviour owned by the component per ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES (focus lifecycle is not state/network orchestration that belongs in hooks).\",\"Hard constraints are pinned, not redesigned: AC-5 guards Escape through the existing document keydown handler and AC-4 guards the detached-opener restore, so Escape/backdrop/close-button semantics stay unchanged while the new behaviour composes with them.\",\"The empty-deps effect is architecturally correct, not incidental: it makes focus entry/return a pure mount/unmount concern immune to onClose identity churn from ChatArea's fresh closures, matching the component's existing body-scroll-lock effect pattern and surviving StrictMode's dev double-invoke.\",\"Convergence improves on the multi-ticket horizon: real keyboard-accessibility behaviour is added behind an unchanged interface (a deeper module), no declared no-growth file grows, and nothing here forecloses a deliberate shared focus seam if a third modal ever justifies one.\"],\"required_changes\":[],\"source_files\":[\"app/frontend/src/App.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-handleCitationClick.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-refreshConversationsRef.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-strictmode-first-send.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/AddVideoModal.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Message.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/main.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/pages/AdminVideos.tsx\"],\"version\":\"1.0\"}\n"},"architecture-governor.raw.json":{"sha256":"70c7b2ff338f4d6eddd0d9df970bcf8e3e5dbad9d3ef2d4d9f98323fa9927a78","text":"{\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"decision\": \"proceed\",\n  \"convergence\": \"improves\",\n  \"principles\": [\n    \"ARCH-DEEP-MODULES\",\n    \"ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES\"\n  ],\n  \"migrations\": [\n    \"MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS\"\n  ],\n  \"debts\": [\n    \"DEBT-CHAT-AREA\"\n  ],\n  \"rationale\": [\n    \"Named, testable seam: AC-1/AC-2/AC-4 map to CitationModal's mount-effect-with-cleanup, provable through the public interface (render, unmount, document.activeElement) without reaching into internals.\",\n    \"Behaviour sits behind the seam, not in front of it: opener capture, Close-button focus and the detached-opener guard all live inside CitationModal's lifecycle; the caller needs no new props, callbacks or state, so no orchestration is pushed onto ChatArea.\",\n    \"Interface stays small: CitationModal's public signature is unchanged, no new exports, refs or configuration knobs are exposed, and no new npm dependency is introduced.\",\n    \"The design extends the existing deep module rather than adding a parallel one: planned_files is CitationModal.tsx only, allowed_new_files is empty, and it follows AddVideoModal's established focus-on-open precedent instead of inventing a new abstraction.\",\n    \"No parallel-seam risk: no focus-return hook or util exists in app/frontend/src/hooks or lib (verified), and inline modal-lifecycle focus is the codebase's existing pattern; a one-off useFocusReturn hook for a single caller would be a speculative abstraction under ARCH-DEEP-MODULES.\",\n    \"DEBT-CHAT-AREA and MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS are respected: ChatArea.tsx and Message.tsx are untouched; had opener capture/restore been pushed into ChatArea, it would have grown the no-growth hotspot and worked against the active migration.\",\n    \"Layer direction intact: CitationModal stays in frontend-components using only React built-ins, adds no import edges, and keeps UI behaviour owned by the component per ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES (focus lifecycle is not state/network orchestration that belongs in hooks).\",\n    \"Hard constraints are pinned, not redesigned: AC-5 guards Escape through the existing document keydown handler and AC-4 guards the detached-opener restore, so Escape/backdrop/close-button semantics stay unchanged while the new behaviour composes with them.\",\n    \"The empty-deps effect is architecturally correct, not incidental: it makes focus entry/return a pure mount/unmount concern immune to onClose identity churn from ChatArea's fresh closures, matching the component's existing body-scroll-lock effect pattern and surviving StrictMode's dev double-invoke.\",\n    \"Convergence improves on the multi-ticket horizon: real keyboard-accessibility behaviour is added behind an unchanged interface (a deeper module), no declared no-growth file grows, and nothing here forecloses a deliberate shared focus seam if a third modal ever justifies one.\"\n  ],\n  \"required_changes\": [],\n  \"notes\": \"Policy sets copied verbatim from the invocation context after recomputation: every context/planned file sits under app/frontend/src (ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES, ARCH-DEEP-MODULES); ChatArea.tsx in context.files triggers MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS and DEBT-CHAT-AREA; no backend or factory policy scope overlaps. Judged against deep-module method: the module is deep (focus entry + return + guard behind one unchanged component interface, testable via activeElement), callers do not orchestrate, and the existing AddVideoModal focus-on-open precedent is widened-in-place rather than cloned. Advisory only, carried in the contract's risk list and confirmed consistent with the code: the StrictMode double-invoke requires opener capture inside the effect invocation paired with its own cleanup (not a ref captured outside the effect cycle), the deps array must remain empty so fresh onClose closures never re-capture the opener, and jsdom tests must establish focus with explicit element.focus() since fireEvent.click does not move focus. The Tab-travel gap (no focus trap) is explicitly out of scope and out of this gate's remit; if a future ticket adds containment, that is the moment to consider a shared focus seam deliberately. Escape handler keeps its [onClose] deps while the new focus effect uses [] — two effects, two concerns, one component.\"\n}\n"},"context.enriched.json":{"sha256":"9ac0a300f2fe7684aaf77a9e536a0e686b959057cc0775a0cd554d06dbcf2f10","text":"{\"adrs\":[],\"callers\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleCitationClick\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx#citationChip\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/App.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/pages/AdminVideos.tsx\"],\"contract_sha256\":\"1e4872c41bedc71ca8e0210062d87b20f0b7c8a12d8843d5ada96bdcef2ef63b\",\"deterministic_impact\":{\"callers\":[\"app/frontend/src/App.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/pages/AdminVideos.tsx\"],\"derived_files\":[\"app/frontend/src/App.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-refreshConversationsRef.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-strictmode-first-send.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Message.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/pages/AdminVideos.tsx\"],\"mode\":\"context\",\"public_interfaces\":[{\"file\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx\",\"language\":\"typescript\",\"line\":9,\"name\":\"formatTimestamp\",\"public\":true},{\"file\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx\",\"language\":\"typescript\",\"line\":16,\"name\":\"CitationModal\",\"public\":true},{\"file\":\"app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx\",\"language\":\"typescript\",\"line\":163,\"name\":\"Message\",\"public\":true},{\"file\":\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx\",\"language\":\"typescript\",\"line\":292,\"name\":\"ChatArea\",\"public\":tr