\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-handleCitationClick.test.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-refreshConversationsRef.test.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-strictmode-first-send.test.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.test.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/components/Message.test.tsx\"],\"version\":\"1.0\"}\n"},"context.raw.json":{"sha256":"eaa821c57fb543498981bb3b9e7c57a3889c65439f668a8361428e90cd84520f","text":"{\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"contract_sha256\": \"1e4872c41bedc71ca8e0210062d87b20f0b7c8a12d8843d5ada96bdcef2ef63b\",\n  \"files\": [\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.test.tsx\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/AddVideoModal.tsx\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-handleCitationClick.test.tsx\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/main.tsx\"\n  ],\n  \"symbols\": [\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleCitationClick\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx#citationChip\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/AddVideoModal.tsx#AddVideoModal\"\n  ],\n  \"callers\": [\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleCitationClick\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx#citationChip\"\n  ],\n  \"tests\": [\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.test.tsx\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-handleCitationClick.test.tsx\"\n  ],\n  \"invariants\": [\n    \"Focus entry and return are implemented entirely within CitationModal's own mount/unmount lifecycle (refs plus one mount effect with cleanup); no new props, callbacks or state are added to CitationModal's callers, and ChatArea's conditional mount of CitationModal (ChatArea.tsx:787-789) is unchanged.\",\n    \"The focus effect uses an empty dependency array and does not re-run when the onClose prop identity changes (ChatArea passes a fresh closure every render); re-running on identity churn would re-capture the wrong opener mid-session.\",\n    \"Existing CitationModal tests that pin Escape close, backdrop close, close-button close, iframe embed src with start/autoplay, the 'Open on YouTube' link href and t param, transcript excerpt rendering with pre-wrap, the Video-unavailable states and body-scroll lock remain green without modification.\",\n    \"Dynamous citations never open the modal (ChatArea routes them directly to lesson_url or the missing-link toast), so neither focus criterion ever applies to them.\",\n    \"The Close (×) button keeps rendering unconditionally in every modal state (including Video-unavailable), since focus entry targets it as the only always-present control.\",\n    \"No focus trap, no inert/aria-hidden on background content and no new npm dependency; Tab may still travel from the modal to background content (accepted residual gap, not an acceptance criterion).\",\n    \"Escape close via the existing document keydown handler, backdrop click close and close-button close are preserved unchanged; video playback, timestamp links and citation routing are untouched.\",\n    \"Authentication, owner-private conversations and the 25 messages per user per 24 hours limit are untouched.\"\n  ],\n  \"adrs\": [],\n  \"history\": [],\n  \"notes\": \"Evidence gathered: CitationModal.tsx already has a role='dialog' aria-label='Video citation' backdrop, an unconditional Close button (aria-label 'Close', lines 78-84) that is the only control rendered in every modal state including Video-unavailable, an existing document keydown Escape effect (lines 39-45, deps [onClose]) and a body-scroll-lock effect with empty deps (lines 48-53). The change adds one more empty-deps mount effect with cleanup plus a close-button ref and an opener capture; it must follow AddVideoModal.tsx's focus-on-open effect style (lines 13-22) for the biome formatter gate. Message.tsx#citationChip renders each citation as a native <button> (lines 51-74), so chips are already keyboard-focusable and AC-3 needs no Message change. ChatArea.tsx mounts CitationModal conditionally at lines 787-789 with onClose={() => setSelectedCitation(null)}; handleCitationClick (lines 443-459) routes Dynamous citations away from the modal (issue #247 toast, issue #216 window.open) — both paths pinned by app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-handleCitationClick.test.tsx which must stay green. main.tsx renders <React.StrictMode>, so the effect is double-invoked mount→cleanup→mount in dev; opener capture and restore must live inside the same effect invocation. Vitest environment is jsdom (vitest.config.ts:13); fireEvent.click does not move focus there, so tests must establish focus with explicit element.focus(). No ADR directory exists in the repo (docs/agents contains domain.md, issue-tracker.md, matt-skills.md; none govern frontend layering beyond CLAUDE.md conventions). Test files listed under tests are where new checkpoints belong; they are not production files. No dependencies declared in the contract, so no manifest or lockfile is in scope.\"\n}\n"},"design.json":{"sha256":"b12a6976956859c6e8671faf313c3183da72f643b7badf40fad1b106dbbacd02","text":"{\"ac_mapping\":{\"AC-1\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect with cleanup: focus entry + focus return)\"],\"AC-2\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect with cleanup: focus entry + focus return)\"],\"AC-3\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleCitationClick (chip activation opens CitationModal; Escape closes it)\"],\"AC-4\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect with cleanup: focus entry + focus return)\"],\"AC-5\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (document keydown Escape handler)\"]},\"allowed_new_files\":[],\"context_sha256\":\"674a06476636c493cb59dc93f93505743dff5b622665f990f3e4107dcff7d7fd\",\"contract_sha256\":\"1e4872c41bedc71ca8e0210062d87b20f0b7c8a12d8843d5ada96bdcef2ef63b\",\"data_flows\":[\"citation chip (native <button> in Message.tsx) -> ChatArea.handleCitationClick -> setSelectedCitation -> CitationModal mounts (ChatArea.tsx:787-789)\",\"document.activeElement at mount -> CitationModal mount effect -> opener captured in effect-local variable, focus moved to Close button ref\",\"Escape keydown / Close button click / backdrop click -> onClose -> CitationModal unmounts -> effect cleanup focuses opener when opener.isConnected, else no-op (focus falls back to body)\"],\"invariants\":[\"Opening the modal moves keyboard focus to the Close button (role button, accessible name 'Close') inside the role='dialog' element labelled 'Video citation'.\",\"Closing via any path (Escape, Close button, backdrop click) restores focus to the element focused immediately before the modal opened, when that element remains in the document; when it does not, closing completes without throwing and activeElement falls back to the browser default (body).\",\"The focus effect uses an empty dependency array; it never re-runs on onClose identity churn (ChatArea passes a fresh closure every render).\",\"Existing close paths, the document keydown Escape handler, iframe embed src with start/autoplay, the 'Open on YouTube' link, transcript pre-wrap rendering, Video-unavailable states and the body-scroll lock are unchanged.\",\"The Close button keeps rendering unconditionally in every modal state (including Video-unavailable) since focus entry targets it as the only always-present control.\",\"No new props, callbacks, state or npm dependencies for CitationModal or its callers; no focus trap, no inert/aria-hidden on background content; ChatArea.tsx and Message.tsx are not modified.\",\"Dynamous citations never open the modal, so focus entry/return never applies to them.\",\"Focus management survives React StrictMode's dev double-invoke (mount→cleanup→mount re-captures the correct opener) because opener capture, Close-button focus and restore all live in one empty-deps effect invocation paired with its own cleanup.\"],\"modules\":[\"CitationModal (app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx)\"],\"planned_files\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx\"],\"public_interfaces\":[\"CitationModal(props: { citation: Citation; onClose: () => void }) -> JSX.Element (signature unchanged; focus management is internal)\"],\"seams\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect with cleanup: focus entry + focus return)\",\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (document keydown Escape handler)\",\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleCitationClick (chip activation opens CitationModal; Escape closes it)\"],\"version\":\"1.0\"}\n"},"design.raw.json":{"sha256":"d392840a0e93a28c4ecc18c15897764b6e5847d5fdef87d68da88f22d27ede2b","text":"{\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"modules\": [\n    \"CitationModal (app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx)\"\n  ],\n  \"seams\": [\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect with cleanup: focus entry + focus return)\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (document keydown Escape handler)\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleCitationClick (chip activation opens CitationModal; Escape closes it)\"\n  ],\n  \"public_interfaces\": [\n    \"CitationModal(props: { citation: Citation; onClose: () => void }) -> JSX.Element (signature unchanged; focus management is internal)\"\n  ],\n  \"invariants\": [\n    \"Opening the modal moves keyboard focus to the Close button (role button, accessible name 'Close') inside the role='dialog' element labelled 'Video citation'.\",\n    \"Closing via any path (Escape, Close button, backdrop click) restores focus to the element focused immediately before the modal opened, when that element remains in the document; when it does not, closing completes without throwing and activeElement falls back to the browser default (body).\",\n    \"The focus effect uses an empty dependency array; it never re-runs on onClose identity churn (ChatArea passes a fresh closure every render).\",\n    \"Existing close paths, the document keydown Escape handler, iframe embed src with start/autoplay, the 'Open on YouTube' link, transcript pre-wrap rendering, Video-unavailable states and the body-scroll lock are unchanged.\",\n    \"The Close button keeps rendering unconditionally in every modal state (including Video-unavailable) since focus entry targets it as the only always-present control.\",\n    \"No new props, callbacks, state or npm dependencies for CitationModal or its callers; no focus trap, no inert/aria-hidden on background content; ChatArea.tsx and Message.tsx are not modified.\",\n    \"Dynamous citations never open the modal, so focus entry/return never applies to them.\",\n    \"Focus management survives React StrictMode's dev double-invoke (mount→cleanup→mount re-captures the correct opener) because opener capture, Close-button focus and restore all live in one empty-deps effect invocation paired with its own cleanup.\"\n  ],\n  \"data_flows\": [\n    \"citation chip (native <button> in Message.tsx) -> ChatArea.handleCitationClick -> setSelectedCitation -> CitationModal mounts (ChatArea.tsx:787-789)\",\n    \"document.activeElement at mount -> CitationModal mount effect -> opener captured in effect-local variable, focus moved to Close button ref\",\n    \"Escape keydown / Close button click / backdrop click -> onClose -> CitationModal unmounts -> effect cleanup focuses opener when opener.isConnected, else no-op (focus falls back to body)\"\n  ],\n  \"ac_mapping\": {\n    \"AC-1\": [\n      \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect with cleanup: focus entry + focus return)\"\n    ],\n    \"AC-2\": [\n      \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect with cleanup: focus entry + focus return)\"\n    ],\n    \"AC-3\": [\n      \"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleCitationClick (chip activation opens CitationModal; Escape closes it)\"\n    ],\n    \"AC-4\": [\n      \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect with cleanup: focus entry + focus return)\"\n    ],\n    \"AC-5\": [\n      \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (document keydown Escape handler)\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"planned_files\": [\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx\"\n  ],\n  \"allowed_new_files\": [],\n  \"notes\": \"Smallest deep-module design: all behaviour behind CitationModal's existing public interface, one production file touched, no new files, no caller changes. Implementation shape: add a useRef<HTMLButtonElement> attached to the existing Close button, plus one useEffect with [] deps that (a) captures document.activeElement into an effect-local variable at mount, (b) focuses closeButtonRef.current, and whose cleanup restores focus to the opener only when it is still connected (opener instanceof HTMLElement && opener.isConnected); a detached opener is skipped so closing never throws and focus falls back to body (AC-4 guard). This mirrors AddVideoModal.tsx's focus-on-open effect style for the biome formatter gate. AC-3 requires no production change: the chip is already a native <button>, ChatArea's conditional mount is untouched, and Escape already unmounts the modal — the integration checkpoint belongs in app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-handleCitationClick.test.tsx (focus the chip explicitly, activate it, assert Close focused, Escape, assert chip refocused). Focus entry/return/detached-guard checkpoints belong in app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.test.tsx alongside the unchanged existing tests; jsdom needs explicit element.focus() since fireEvent.click does not move focus. No dependencies declared, so no manifest or lockfile is planned. Ceiling: no focus trap and no Tab containment (accepted residual gap per contract out_of_scope); if containment is ever required it is a separate contract.\"\n}\n"},"frontier.json":{"sha256":"4af569e604a9467d57deea5eb3638a085a72b0eeddbe4f8dd0c98a46e0fcd7d2","text":"{\"accepted\":true,\"blockers\":[{\"issue\":181,\"state\":\"CLOSED\"}],\"issue\":189,\"ready\":true,\"ticket_sha256\":\"50959c913674f89ffb3c987db66dae89b28eab71b0d68ecb1ec2fb803f8c0937\",\"version\":\"1.0\"}\n"},"issue-frontier.json":{"sha256":"e5b9352b104e5b6627a31f63b155f08b94e9a501450c78f2b4e2996df27cb52a","text":"{\"blockers\":[{\"issue\":181,\"state\":\"CLOSED\"}],\"fetched_at\":\"2026-09-16T10:25:03Z\",\"issue\":{\"author\":{\"is_bot\":true,\"login\":\"app/shaishibear-dark-factory\"},\"body\":\"<!-- dark-factory-programme:d809b087a48a5d3a634286dc5f303d90ce119139a799ace0a122a7e244766b00:keyboard -->\\n\\nViewers can read the cited transcript and use the citation modal with the keyboard.\\n\\nSpecification: citation-inspection v1\\nSpecification SHA256: 2ebd0a37d772950d9364c1178f7c6330c6c0cd12367a479ef1eebc7a66f0bbb5\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- focus-entry (keyboard): Opening the citation modal moves keyboard focus to a usable control inside it.\\n- focus-return (keyboard): Closing the citation modal returns keyboard focus to the opener when it remains in the document.\\n\\n## Hard constraints\\n- Preserve existing video playback, timestamp links, Escape, close-button and backdrop close behavior.\\n- Preserve authentication, owner-private conversations and the 25 messages per user per 24 hours limit.\\n- All existing independent proof and permission rules remain mandatory.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No new content sources, sharing, auth changes, factory authority changes or external dependencies.\\n\\nBlocked by: #181\\n\\nThis is a compiled programme candidate. Normal triage and all existing factory proof and permission rules apply.\\n\",\"labels\":[{\"color\":\"5319E7\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory control state\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACyJrubg\",\"name\":\"factory:accepted\"},{\"color\":\"fbca04\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory triage label\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACzxETvQ\",\"name\":\"priority:medium\"},{\"color\":\"a2eeef\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory triage label\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACzxEU9Q\",\"name\":\"type:enhancement\"}],\"number\":189,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"Citation inspection [keyboard]\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-16T10:23:31Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ShaishiBear/dark-factory-2.0/issues/189\"},\"version\":\"1.0\"}\n"},"issue.json":{"sha256":"8ba5e4f585355e4bcb42c5580c0c56cac80d0036833a2905c2645d0a21b5a197","text":"{\"author\":{\"is_bot\":true,\"login\":\"app/shaishibear-dark-factory\"},\"body\":\"<!-- dark-factory-programme:d809b087a48a5d3a634286dc5f303d90ce119139a799ace0a122a7e244766b00:keyboard -->\\n\\nViewers can read the cited transcript and use the citation modal with the keyboard.\\n\\nSpecification: citation-inspection v1\\nSpecification SHA256: 2ebd0a37d772950d9364c1178f7c6330c6c0cd12367a479ef1eebc7a66f0bbb5\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- focus-entry (keyboard): Opening the citation modal moves keyboard focus to a usable control inside it.\\n- focus-return (keyboard): Closing the citation modal returns keyboard focus to the opener when it remains in the document.\\n\\n## Hard constraints\\n- Preserve existing video playback, timestamp links, Escape, close-button and backdrop close behavior.\\n- Preserve authentication, owner-private conversations and the 25 messages per user per 24 hours limit.\\n- All existing independent proof and permission rules remain mandatory.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No new content sources, sharing, auth changes, factory authority changes or external dependencies.\\n\\nBlocked by: #181\\n\\nThis is a compiled programme candidate. Normal triage and all existing factory proof and permission rules apply.\\n\",\"labels\":[{\"color\":\"5319E7\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory control state\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACyJrubg\",\"name\":\"factory:accepted\"},{\"color\":\"fbca04\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory triage label\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACzxETvQ\",\"name\":\"priority:medium\"},{\"color\":\"a2eeef\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory triage label\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACzxEU9Q\",\"name\":\"type:enhancement\"}],\"number\":189,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"Citation inspection [keyboard]\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-16T10:23:31Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ShaishiBear/dark-factory-2.0/issues/189\"}\n"},"task-contract.json":{"sha256":"1e4872c41bedc71ca8e0210062d87b20f0b7c8a12d8843d5ada96bdcef2ef63b","text":"{\"ambiguities\":[],\"behaviors\":[{\"given\":\"the citation modal is not mounted and some element in the document has keyboard focus\",\"id\":\"AC-1\",\"seam\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect)\",\"then\":\"keyboard focus moves off the previously focused element and onto the modal's Close button (role button, accessible name 'Close'), which sits inside the role='dialog' element labelled 'Video citation'\",\"when\":\"the citation modal opens (CitationModal mounts)\"},{\"given\":\"an element has keyboard focus in the document and the citation modal is then opened\",\"id\":\"AC-2\",\"seam\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect cleanup)\",\"then\":\"keyboard focus is restored to the element that was focused immediately before the modal opened, when that element remains in the document\",\"when\":\"the modal closes via any close path (Escape, the Close button, or the backdrop click), unmounting CitationModal\"},{\"given\":\"keyboard focus is on a YouTube citation chip rendered by Message in the message list\",\"id\":\"AC-3\",\"seam\":\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleCitationClick (chip activation opens CitationModal; Escape closes it)\",\"then\":\"while the modal is open keyboard focus is inside the modal (off the chip), and after Escape the modal is gone and keyboard focus is back on that same citation chip\",\"when\":\"the chip is activated so the citation modal opens, and the modal is then closed with Escape\"},{\"given\":\"the citation modal is open and the element that had focus before it opened has since been removed from the document\",\"id\":\"AC-4\",\"kind\":\"guard\",\"seam\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (unmount cleanup)\",\"then\":\"closing completes without throwing and focus is not forced onto a detached node (document.activeElement falls back to the browser default, body) — the AC's 'when it remains in the document' conditional, pinned so a naive restore cannot regress it\",\"when\":\"the modal closes\"},{\"given\":\"the citation modal is open and keyboard focus is on its Close button (the entry position this change introduces)\",\"id\":\"AC-5\",\"kind\":\"guard\",\"seam\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (document keydown Escape handler)\",\"then\":\"the modal closes via the existing document keydown handler (onClose invoked) — Escape behaviour is unchanged by the new focus management\",\"when\":\"Escape is pressed\"}],\"dependencies\":[],\"invariants\":[\"Focus entry and return are implemented entirely within CitationModal's own mount/unmount lifecycle (refs plus one mount effect with cleanup); no new props, callbacks or state are added to CitationModal's callers, and ChatArea's conditional mount of CitationModal (ChatArea.tsx:787-789) is unchanged.\",\"The focus effect uses an empty dependency array and does not re-run when the onClose prop identity changes (ChatArea passes a fresh closure every render); re-running on identity churn would re-capture the wrong opener mid-session.\",\"Existing CitationModal tests that pin Escape close, backdrop close, close-button close, iframe embed src with start/autoplay, the 'Open on YouTube' link href and t param, transcript excerpt rendering with pre-wrap, the Video-unavailable states and body-scroll lock remain green without modification.\",\"Dynamous citations never open the modal (ChatArea routes them directly to lesson_url or the missing-link toast), so neither focus criterion ever applies to them.\",\"The Close (×) button keeps rendering unconditionally in every modal state (including Video-unavailable), since focus entry targets it as the only always-present control.\",\"No focus trap, no inert/aria-hidden on background content and no new npm dependency; Tab may still travel from the modal to background content (accepted residual gap, not an acceptance criterion).\",\"Authentication, owner-private conversations and the 25 messages per user per 24 hours limit are untouched.\"],\"issue\":{\"number\":189,\"title\":\"Citation inspection [keyboard]\"},\"out_of_scope\":[\"Tab containment / focus trap, inert or aria-hidden on background content, and any focus-trap library (the issue forbids new external dependencies and containment is not an acceptance criterion).\",\"The Dynamous citation path (direct lesson_url open and missing-link toast, issue #247).\",\"New content sources, sharing, auth changes, factory authority changes and external dependencies (issue statement).\",\"Modal visual design, video playback, timestamp links and the existing Escape / close-button / backdrop close semantics — preserved behaviour, not redesigned.\",\"Authentication, owner-private conversations and the 25-messages-per-user-per-24-hours limit.\",\"Backend, RAG pipeline and deployment files.\"],\"risks\":[\"React StrictMode (main.tsx) double-invokes effects mount→cleanup→mount in dev; the single empty-deps effect must capture the opener, focus the Close button, and restore in its own cleanup so the simulated remount re-captures the correct opener.\",\"onClose identity churn: ChatArea passes a new closure every render, so keying the focus effect on onClose would re-capture document.activeElement mid-session (the Close button) and corrupt focus-return; reviewers should check the deps array specifically.\",\"jsdom focus semantics: fireEvent.click does not move focus in jsdom, so checkpoints must establish focus with explicit element.focus(); a RED expectation declared from a click-based assumption will not match actual output.\",\"Streaming re-renders can unmount the opener chip while the modal is open, making focus-return no-op to body — this is inside the AC's conditional, not a defect, and is pinned by the opener-removed guard.\",\"Focus entry targets the Close button, which is only correct while it renders unconditionally; today it does, including the Video-unavailable states, and nothing in this build changes that.\",\"Formatter gate: the kernel applies biome format on declared files; keep the new effect's style consistent with AddVideoModal.tsx's focus-on-open effect to avoid burning the hand-back on formatting.\"],\"summary\":\"Add keyboard focus management to CitationModal: opening the modal moves keyboard focus to the modal's Close button (a usable control inside the dialog), and closing it returns keyboard focus to the element that opened it when that element remains in the document. Implemented entirely within CitationModal's own mount/unmount lifecycle; no changes to callers, close paths, video playback, timestamp links or citation routing.\",\"version\":\"2.0\"}\n"},"task-contract.raw.json":{"sha256":"21110e2290b5771f26ae5f7638f9a841d4c9fca8a35e32b4ad7c407913fa459f","text":"{\n  \"version\": \"2.0\",\n  \"issue\": {\n    \"number\": 189,\n    \"title\": \"Citation inspection [keyboard]\"\n  },\n  \"summary\": \"Add keyboard focus management to CitationModal: opening the modal moves keyboard focus to the modal's Close button (a usable control inside the dialog), and closing it returns keyboard focus to the element that opened it when that element remains in the document. Implemented entirely within CitationModal's own mount/unmount lifecycle; no changes to callers, close paths, video playback, timestamp links or citation routing.\",\n  \"behaviors\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-1\",\n      \"given\": \"the citation modal is not mounted and some element in the document has keyboard focus\",\n      \"when\": \"the citation modal opens (CitationModal mounts)\",\n      \"then\": \"keyboard focus moves off the previously focused element and onto the modal's Close button (role button, accessible name 'Close'), which sits inside the role='dialog' element labelled 'Video citation'\",\n      \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-2\",\n      \"given\": \"an element has keyboard focus in the document and the citation modal is then opened\",\n      \"when\": \"the modal closes via any close path (Escape, the Close button, or the backdrop click), unmounting CitationModal\",\n      \"then\": \"keyboard focus is restored to the element that was focused immediately before the modal opened, when that element remains in the document\",\n      \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect cleanup)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-3\",\n      \"given\": \"keyboard focus is on a YouTube citation chip rendered by Message in the message list\",\n      \"when\": \"the chip is activated so the citation modal opens, and the modal is then closed with Escape\",\n      \"then\": \"while the modal is open keyboard focus is inside the modal (off the chip), and after Escape the modal is gone and keyboard focus is back on that same citation chip\",\n      \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleCitationClick (chip activation opens CitationModal; Escape closes it)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-4\",\n      \"kind\": \"guard\",\n      \"given\": \"the citation modal is open and the element that had focus before it opened has since been removed from the document\",\n      \"when\": \"the modal closes\",\n      \"then\": \"closing completes without throwing and focus is not forced onto a detached node (document.activeElement falls back to the browser default, body) — the AC's 'when it remains in the document' conditional, pinned so a naive restore cannot regress it\",\n      \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (unmount cleanup)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-5\",\n      \"kind\": \"guard\",\n      \"given\": \"the citation modal is open and keyboard focus is on its Close button (the entry position this change introduces)\",\n      \"when\": \"Escape is pressed\",\n      \"then\": \"the modal closes via the existing document keydown handler (onClose invoked) — Escape behaviour is unchanged by the new focus management\",\n      \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (document keydown Escape handler)\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"invariants\": [\n    \"Focus entry and return are implemented entirely within CitationModal's own mount/unmount lifecycle (refs plus one mount effect with cleanup); no new props, callbacks or state are added to CitationModal's callers, and ChatArea's conditional mount of CitationModal (ChatArea.tsx:787-789) is unchanged.\",\n    \"The focus effect uses an empty dependency array and does not re-run when the onClose prop identity changes (ChatArea passes a fresh closure every render); re-running on identity churn would re-capture the wrong opener mid-session.\",\n    \"Existing CitationModal tests that pin Escape close, backdrop close, close-button close, iframe embed src with start/autoplay, the 'Open on YouTube' link href and t param, transcript excerpt rendering with pre-wrap, the Video-unavailable states and body-scroll lock remain green without modification.\",\n    \"Dynamous citations never open the modal (ChatArea routes them directly to lesson_url or the missing-link toast), so neither focus criterion ever applies to them.\",\n    \"The Close (×) button keeps rendering unconditionally in every modal state (including Video-unavailable), since focus entry targets it as the only always-present control.\",\n    \"No focus trap, no inert/aria-hidden on background content and no new npm dependency; Tab may still travel from the modal to background content (accepted residual gap, not an acceptance criterion).\",\n    \"Authentication, owner-private conversations and the 25 messages per user per 24 hours limit are untouched.\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"Tab containment / focus trap, inert or aria-hidden on background content, and any focus-trap library (the issue forbids new external dependencies and containment is not an acceptance criterion).\",\n    \"The Dynamous citation path (direct lesson_url open and missing-link toast, issue #247).\",\n    \"New content sources, sharing, auth changes, factory authority changes and external dependencies (issue statement).\",\n    \"Modal visual design, video playback, timestamp links and the existing Escape / close-button / backdrop close semantics — preserved behaviour, not redesigned.\",\n    \"Authentication, owner-private conversations and the 25-messages-per-user-per-24-hours limit.\",\n    \"Backend, RAG pipeline and deployment files.\"\n  ],\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"React StrictMode (main.tsx) double-invokes effects mount→cleanup→mount in dev; the single empty-deps effect must capture the opener, focus the Close button, and restore in its own cleanup so the simulated remount re-captures the correct opener.\",\n    \"onClose identity churn: ChatArea passes a new closure every render, so keying the focus effect on onClose would re-capture document.activeElement mid-session (the Close button) and corrupt focus-return; reviewers should check the deps array specifically.\",\n    \"jsdom focus semantics: fireEvent.click does not move focus in jsdom, so checkpoints must establish focus with explicit element.focus(); a RED expectation declared from a click-based assumption will not match actual output.\",\n    \"Streaming re-renders can unmount the opener chip while the modal is open, making focus-return no-op to body — this is inside the AC's conditional, not a defect, and is pinned by the opener-removed guard.\",\n    \"Focus entry targets the Close button, which is only correct while it renders unconditionally; today it does, including the Video-unavailable states, and nothing in this build changes that.\",\n    \"Formatter gate: the kernel applies biome format on declared files; keep the new effect's style consistent with AddVideoModal.tsx's focus-on-open effect to avoid burning the hand-back on formatting.\"\n  ],\n  \"ambiguities\": [],\n  \"dependencies\": []\n}\n"},"ticket.json":{"sha256":"50959c913674f89ffb3c987db66dae89b28eab71b0d68ecb1ec2fb803f8c0937","text":"{\"acceptance\":[\"AC-1\",\"AC-2\",\"AC-3\",\"AC-4\",\"AC-5\"],\"body_sha256\":\"c9ab4b6c10b1bc2e22dce3602ffde023c2d6c26cb885a9df12e56b7c665ec56a\",\"contract_sha256\":\"1e4872c41bedc71ca8e0210062d87b20f0b7c8a12d8843d5ada96bdcef2ef63b\",\"issue\":189,\"parent\":null,\"test_seams\":{\"AC-1\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect)\",\"AC-2\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect cleanup)\",\"AC-3\":\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleCitationClick (chip activation opens CitationModal; Escape closes it)\",\"AC-4\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (unmount cleanup)\",\"AC-5\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (document keydown Escape handler)\"},\"title\":\"Citation inspection [keyboard]\",\"version\":\"1.0\"}\n"}},"base_sha":"c52f87dce735444383cb6be3b36e5a8e0cbff772","issue":189,"issue_sha256":"ee04b5def8b555b9255e81078bb4c0444cd97041719b3cd3792efab4e1010628","kernel_commit":"c52f87dce735444383cb6be3b36e5a8e0cbff772","note_ref":"refs/notes/dark-factory-carry","policy_sha256":"784f2061717e89d5a14234d324802cf69fc9620463ad723288757b302c6fb860","run_id":"issue-189-a1-b2f0c75df2","version":"1.0","written_at":"2026-09-16T10:40:25Z"}
